WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.958 --> 00:00:31.708
<b>In the previous verse,</b>

2
00:00:31.708 --> 00:00:37.708
<b>we learned how the Vedas are</b>
<b>like a forest of infinite knowledge,</b>

3
00:00:37.708 --> 00:00:41.666
<b>and people around us offer various opinions.</b>

4
00:00:41.666 --> 00:00:44.000
<b>All this can confuse a person.</b>

5
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.000
<b>We also learned how important it is to </b>
<b>emerge from this forest of thoughts.</b>

6
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.666
<b>Now here, Krishna explains</b>

7
00:00:53.666 --> 00:00:56.625
<b>what the experience will be like afterward,</b>

8
00:00:56.625 --> 00:00:59.458
<b>and what will be achieved.</b>

9
00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:01.208
<b>He tells Arjuna</b>

10
00:01:01.208 --> 00:01:03.375
<b>that when your intellect</b>

11
00:01:03.375 --> 00:01:07.333
<b>recognizes the contradictions</b>
<b>in Vedic statements,</b>

12
00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.500
<b>it will become steady.</b>

13
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:13.708
<b>With such a peaceful intellect,</b>
<b>focused concentration</b>

14
00:01:13.708 --> 00:01:16.708
<b>can lead you to the state of Samadhi,</b>

15
00:01:16.708 --> 00:01:17.833
<b>and that is</b>

16
00:01:17.833 --> 00:01:20.166
<b>the attainment of Yoga.</b>

17
00:01:25.041 --> 00:01:27.208
<b>Krishna is explaining here</b>

18
00:01:27.208 --> 00:01:31.916
<b>that as one begins to elevate</b>
<b>their spiritual knowledge,</b>

19
00:01:31.916 --> 00:01:36.416
<b>they notice many contradictions in </b>
<b>previously acquired knowledge.</b>

20
00:01:36.416 --> 00:01:37.250
<b>But</b>

21
00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:40.541
<b>gradually, they also begin to understand</b>

22
00:01:40.541 --> 00:01:45.000
<b>that perhaps the previous knowledge </b>
<b>wasn't entirely wrong</b>

23
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.208
<b>everything was simply according to</b>
<b>a certain level of understanding.</b>

24
00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.708
<b>This is similar</b>

25
00:01:50.708 --> 00:01:55.875
<b>to how you cannot teach advanced </b>
<b>class material to a young child.</b>

26
00:01:55.875 --> 00:02:01.208
<b>At that age, some things must be </b>
<b>taught in very simplified forms.</b>

27
00:02:01.208 --> 00:02:04.541
<b>Now that you're in a higher class,</b>

28
00:02:04.541 --> 00:02:07.208
<b>more intelligent than before,</b>

29
00:02:07.208 --> 00:02:12.875
<b>you understand that what you </b>
<b>learned in childhood was different, </b>

30
00:02:12.875 --> 00:02:13.666
<b>but</b>

31
00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:15.125
<b>not wrong.</b>

32
00:02:15.125 --> 00:02:19.125
<b>It was simply appropriate for that young age.</b>

33
00:02:19.125 --> 00:02:20.000
<b>In this situation,</b>

34
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.791
<b>you move toward new learning </b>
<b>while leaving behind old teachings.</b>

35
00:02:24.791 --> 00:02:29.458
<b>The contradiction between old and </b>
<b>new knowledge doesn't trouble you.</b>

36
00:02:29.458 --> 00:02:30.541
<b>Similarly,</b>

37
00:02:30.541 --> 00:02:34.333
<b>when you reach the higher </b>
<b>levels of Vedic education,</b>

38
00:02:34.333 --> 00:02:39.791
<b>your intellect doesn't get disturbed by</b>
<b>contradictions in previous statements;</b>

39
00:02:39.791 --> 00:02:43.791
<b>your intellect begins to </b>
<b>become steady and peaceful.</b>

40
00:02:43.791 --> 00:02:46.666
<b>This is what's called unwavering intellect.</b>

41
00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:51.583
<b>When you do anything with complete </b>
<b>concentration in this unwavering intellect,</b>

42
00:02:51.583 --> 00:02:54.958
<b>it's called the state of Samadhi.</b>

43
00:02:54.958 --> 00:02:59.833
<b>And such a state of Samadhi will </b>
<b>lead you toward spiritual truth,</b>

44
00:02:59.833 --> 00:03:01.125
<b>and ultimately</b>

45
00:03:01.125 --> 00:03:04.166
<b>bring about the realization of the Supreme.</b>

46
00:03:08.541 --> 00:03:15.958
<b>Maintaining single-minded focus on </b>
<b>your life goals can be challenging.</b>

47
00:03:15.958 --> 00:03:17.625
<b>Especially</b>

48
00:03:17.625 --> 00:03:23.333
<b>when surrounded by</b>
<b>countless sensory temptations,</b>

49
00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:30.875
<b>and people insisting their suggestions </b>
<b>and opinions are right.</b>

50
00:03:30.875 --> 00:03:32.208
<b>In such situations,</b>

51
00:03:32.208 --> 00:03:35.583
<b>one often becomes confused.</b>

52
00:03:35.583 --> 00:03:38.125
<b>Like a child at a fair,</b>

53
00:03:38.125 --> 00:03:40.375
<b>attracted to everything,</b>

54
00:03:40.375 --> 00:03:42.791
<b>wanting to experience it all,</b>

55
00:03:42.791 --> 00:03:47.583
<b>yearning to taste every delicious treat.</b>

56
00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:49.041
<b>But</b>

57
00:03:49.041 --> 00:03:54.916
<b>if that same child grows up </b>
<b>to become an athlete,</b>

58
00:03:54.916 --> 00:04:02.791
<b>they'll control their tastes </b>
<b>and eat only what's healthy.</b>

59
00:04:02.791 --> 00:04:04.166
<b>Moreover,</b>

60
00:04:04.166 --> 00:04:09.750
<b>if they're determined to</b>
<b>achieve excellence in their sport,</b>

61
00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:15.916
<b>other temptations won't distract them either.</b>

62
00:04:15.916 --> 00:04:21.708
<b>They'll weigh every action</b>
<b>against a single question</b>

63
00:04:21.708 --> 00:04:26.583
<b>Is this bringing me closer to my goals?</b>

64
00:04:26.583 --> 00:04:28.875
<b>This is concentration.</b>

65
00:04:28.875 --> 00:04:35.000
<b>Moving forward, absorbed in </b>
<b>one direction with body and mind.</b>

66
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.375
<b>Similarly,</b>

67
00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:39.458
<b>as your spiritual level rises</b>

68
00:04:39.458 --> 00:04:43.375
<b>and you begin to understand </b>
<b>your spiritual truth, </b>

69
00:04:43.375 --> 00:04:46.625
<b>you realize</b>

70
00:04:46.625 --> 00:04:52.208
<b>your life's purpose is far higher.</b>

71
00:04:52.208 --> 00:04:56.208
<b>It's not just about worldly achievement,</b>

72
00:04:56.208 --> 00:04:56.916
<b>but</b>

73
00:04:56.916 --> 00:05:02.625
<b>about liberation from many bondages.</b>

74
00:05:02.625 --> 00:05:05.291
<b>Once this awareness dawns,</b>

75
00:05:05.291 --> 00:05:12.916
<b>no circumstance can succeed </b>
<b>in destabilizing your mind.</b>

76
00:05:12.916 --> 00:05:17.000
<b>This indeed is unwavering intellect.</b>

77
00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:25.250
<b>This material world</b>

78
00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:27.416
<b>is highly alluring.</b>

79
00:05:27.416 --> 00:05:29.291
<b>Countless attractions.</b>

80
00:05:29.291 --> 00:05:31.208
<b>Here's a promise of pleasure,</b>

81
00:05:31.208 --> 00:05:33.083
<b>there of a bright future,</b>

82
00:05:33.083 --> 00:05:37.541
<b>and somewhere else of supreme happiness.</b>

83
00:05:37.541 --> 00:05:48.125
<b>One leaves one attraction to chase another, </b>
<b>and frustrated, pursues a third.</b>

84
00:05:48.125 --> 00:05:51.333
<b>Like someone confused by a mirage,</b>

85
00:05:51.333 --> 00:05:56.125
<b>seeing water reflections everywhere.</b>

86
00:05:56.125 --> 00:06:04.250
<b>Chasing life's mirages, one eventually tires,</b>

87
00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:05.125
<b>but</b>

88
00:06:05.125 --> 00:06:10.541
<b>everywhere finds only the </b>
<b>dry sand of dissatisfaction,</b>

89
00:06:10.541 --> 00:06:17.125
<b>never the cool water of happiness.</b>

90
00:06:17.125 --> 00:06:19.916
<b>What irony</b>

91
00:06:19.916 --> 00:06:25.250
<b>one searches the world for happiness</b>
<b>that lies hidden within oneself.</b>

92
00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:31.750
<b>Until you accept this truth, </b>
<b>you'll remain disturbed.</b>

93
00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:32.750
<b>But</b>

94
00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:35.833
<b>once this truth is accepted,</b>

95
00:06:35.833 --> 00:06:39.458
<b>it will show you the right path.</b>

96
00:06:39.458 --> 00:06:47.708
<b>Gradually, understanding dawns that worldly</b>
<b>objects are merely means for living,</b>

97
00:06:47.708 --> 00:06:50.958
<b>not life's purpose.</b>

98
00:06:50.958 --> 00:06:56.166
<b>When this happens, worldly temptations fail.</b>

99
00:06:56.166 --> 00:07:02.000
<b>False promises of happiness become </b>
<b>powerless to attract you.</b>

100
00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:06.791
<b>Your intellect becomes steady. </b>
<b>Becomes unwavering.</b>

101
00:07:06.791 --> 00:07:11.375
<b>And when you search within yourself</b>
<b>with this unwavering intellect,</b>

102
00:07:11.375 --> 00:07:13.458
<b>you'll find happiness,</b>

103
00:07:13.458 --> 00:07:18.541
<b>and realize both the self and the Supreme.</b>

104
00:07:18.541 --> 00:07:24.166
<b>And if you're progressing toward </b>
<b>this unwavering intellect,</b>

105
00:07:24.166 --> 00:07:33.333
<b>try through your example to help family</b>
<b>and society realize this truth too.</b>

106
00:07:33.333 --> 00:07:38.875
<b>Helping others is itself a path to happiness.</b>

107
00:07:43.833 --> 00:07:49.541
<b>Every person in a leadership position </b>
<b>in the professional world</b>

108
00:07:49.541 --> 00:07:53.291
<b>must make many important decisions.</b>

109
00:07:53.291 --> 00:07:59.625
<b>If they become influenced by praise or criticism,</b>

110
00:07:59.625 --> 00:08:04.333
<b>they'll never make right decisions.</b>

111
00:08:04.333 --> 00:08:08.208
<b>They must reach a state of mind</b>

112
00:08:08.208 --> 00:08:12.708
<b>where people's words don't affect them,</b>

113
00:08:12.708 --> 00:08:21.000
<b>and they make every decision solely based on</b>
<b>their wisdom and organizational objectives.</b>

114
00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:24.583
<b>This is the state of steadiness.</b>

115
00:08:24.583 --> 00:08:28.666
<b>Where intellect remains unwavering.</b>

116
00:08:28.666 --> 00:08:36.166
<b>In fact, such a person has already </b>
<b>progressed toward Nishkama Karma Yoga.</b>

117
00:08:36.166 --> 00:08:42.083
<b>If you're in such a state of steadiness, maintain it.</b>

118
00:08:42.083 --> 00:08:43.708
<b>And if you're not,</b>

119
00:08:43.708 --> 00:08:51.125
<b>try to reach that state by following </b>
<b>these teachings of the Gita.</b>

